Runtime dependencies bundled with the application
-------------------------------------------------

Self-hosted: every library below is served from this origin, so each IS
redistributed by this product. scripts/build-vendor.mjs makes them from the
pinned npm packages (scripts/vendor-packages.mjs lists how): most are bundled,
with their own dependencies, into one ESM file under public/js/vendor/ or the
site's shared static/vendor/; qrcode-generator and tesseract-wasm are copied as
their packages ship them; pdf.js is kept as it is. Nothing is loaded from a
third-party CDN at runtime, so the application works without any other host
and no page load discloses request metadata to one. All are permissive (MIT,
BSD-2-Clause, Apache-2.0 or Zlib, as stated against each entry below), which
permits this redistribution.

THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/ holds the full licence text of every package and
component shipped, inside the vendored files and outside them: each npm
package's own licence file, verbatim; for the parts that are not npm packages
(pdf.js, Tesseract and Leptonica inside the OCR engine, eng.traineddata,
Tailwind CSS, Material Symbols) the project's own licence file, verbatim; and
for the two packages that ship no licence file (qrcode-generator,
@pdf-lib/fontkit) the MIT text with the copyright line the project gives.
Together with this file it is the record each licence asks for.

