Embedding: fonts are embedded in produced bundles IN FULL, not subset. Verified
rather than assumed: the font stream in an output PDF decompresses to exactly
the byte length of the source .ttf, and pdffonts reports "sub: no". pdf-lib's
embedFont() does not subset unless asked and is never asked here; the jsPDF path
that builds the index has no subsetting to enable. This matters because
subsetting is arguably a modification, which would engage the Reserved Font Name
clauses above; as things stand no font is modified, so no renaming obligation
arises. The cost is size: the default footer font adds about 211 KB (compressed)
to each produced bundle, once, not per page.
